::SECTION_12_WIN32_ABI_AND_DYNAMIC_LINKING::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-WIN-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Dynamic Library Loading & Calling Convention Alignment (LoadLibraryW / GetProcAddress)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Stack pointer corruption (ESP/RSP mismatch) or NULL function-pointer access violation on DLL call"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Loading DLLs from unanchored relative paths (DLL hijacking) or mismatching `__stdcall` vs `__cdecl` typedef signatures."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Load system/local modules using `LoadLibraryExW` with `LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_SYSTEM32` or explicit full paths; verify `GetProcAddress != NULL` and match exact calling conventions."
}

@FAULT_NODE [ERR-WIN-002] {
    DOMAIN          : "Windows Registry Inspection & Handle Lifecycle (RegOpenKeyExW / RegQueryValueExW)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Registry handle leaks, WOW64 32/64-bit hive redirection misses, or non-null-terminated REG_SZ reads"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Querying `HKLM\\Software` without `KEY_WOW64_64KEY` flags, omitting `RegCloseKey()`, or assuming `RegQueryValueExW` guarantees a trailing null terminator."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Specify explicit hive view flags (`KEY_READ | KEY_WOW64_64KEY`), allocate `cbData + sizeof(wchar_t)` to force null termination, and close every opened `HKEY` on all exit paths."
}

::SECTION_13_CATALOG_SIGNING_AND_BUILD_PACKAGING::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-CAT-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Catalog Definition Generation & MakeCAB / SignTool Pipelines (Dark-Com-2-bat.cat)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Unsigned orphan scripts, stale file hashes in `.cat` catalogs, or MakeCAB directive syntax failures"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Hardcoding file lists in `.cdf` manifests instead of enumerating live workspace artifacts, or leaving unquoted paths with spaces in `.ddf` files."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Generate `.cdf` / `.ddf` entries dynamically from verified directory inventories, quote all source paths, and validate signature verification (`signtool verify /pa`) post-build."
}

::SECTION_14_WINSOCK_AND_TLS_SOCKET_TRANSPORT::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-SOCK-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Low-Level Socket I/O & HTTP Framing (dc2ws2 / Winsock2)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Truncated HTTP responses, hanging `recv()` calls, or missing `Content-Length` / chunked-encoding boundary errors"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Assuming a single `recv()` call returns the entire HTTP payload, or omitting `WSAStartup` / `SO_RCVTIMEO` socket timeouts."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Enforce explicit `SO_RCVTIMEO` and `SO_SNDTIMEO` timeouts, loop `send()`/`recv()` until full byte count or EOF is reached, and parse HTTP header boundaries (`\\r\\n\\r\\n`) before body extraction."
}

::MASTER_VERIFICATION_GATE::
@GATE_CHECK_F04 {
    13. ABI_AND_HIVE_GUARD : Anchor DLL paths, match calling conventions, enforce WOW64 registry flags, and force-terminate REG_SZ buffers.
    14. CATALOG_INTEGRITY  : Sync `.cdf`/`.ddf` manifests directly against live workspace files and verify cryptographic signatures post-build.
    15. SOCKET_FRAMING     : Set explicit Winsock send/recv timeouts and loop I/O calls across partial TCP packet boundaries.
}
::AVIS_MANIFEST_END::
